i iterated over it with codex, and i think it is more lightweight to simply use reconfigured child process groups instead of exposing new device mesh arg to bucket config, which i tried and some redundant work in generic scheduler and fqn matching showed up. can you check the current pr again? let me know wdyt.

from codex: 
> The capped communicator is an internal DistMuon transport policy, not bucket configuration. FlexShard already resolves every bucket to the exact 1D redistribution mesh, including its axis, ranks, and rank order, so deriving the child communicator from that bound mesh makes invalid layouts unrepresentable. This preserves all required functionality while avoiding a new public `BucketConfig.mesh` API, duplicate validation, changes to the generic scheduler, and FQN rematching in the TorchTitan wrapper. The result is smaller, safer, and keeps communicator ownership in the component that actually uses it.
